notes:
I found two free drop-in options for toddlers in Halton Hills. Both come off the operators' own pages.

```json
{
  "picks": [
    {
      "name": "Kids & Me drop-in neighbourhood group, Halton Hills Public Library, Acton Branch",
      "age_fit": "families with babies or children up to 6 years of age",
      "when": "Thursdays 1 p.m. to 2:30 p.m.; follows the school calendar (started the second week of September), closed statutory holidays and the December/January break",
      "price": "Free, no registration required",
      "source_name": "Halton Region"
    },
    {
      "name": "EarlyON Child and Family Centres, Halton Hills (Acton and Georgetown)",
      "price": "Free",
      "age_fit": "children from birth to their 6th birthday with a parent or caregiver",
      "source_name": "Links2Care"
    }
  ]
}
```

- **Kids & Me:** The Acton Branch day and time are from Halton Region's own page. The page says the group is led by a public health nurse, an early childhood educator, a child development consultant and a librarian. It runs on a routine of play, snacks and stories.
- **EarlyON:** Links2Care's page says the programs run weekdays, weekends and evenings, in person as drop-in or registered sessions. I could not read the current schedule, so no day or time is listed for it. The Acton location is the library at 17 River Street, and Georgetown is also listed.
- **Left out:** The Halton Hills Gymnastics Centre has a preschool drop-in for children under 4, but it costs $15 per family, so it isn't free. Its page also gives two different start dates (September 15 and October 9).
